This paper investigates the existence of standardized ground states for the following biharmonic Choquard type equation \begin{align*}
\begin{split}
\left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
\Delta^2u-\beta\Delta u=\lambda u+\left(\int_{\mathbb{R}^4}\frac{u^2dx\right)u^{\phi-2},\quad u>0\text{ in } \Omega,\\
\frac{\partial\Delta u}{\partial n}=0,\quad \text{on } \partial\Omega,
\end{array}
\right.
\end{split}
\end{align*} where $\Omega$ is a bounded domain in $\mathbb{R}^4$ with smooth boundary, $\beta\geq 0$, $\lambda\in\mathbb{R}$, and $\phi$ satisfies $1<\phi\leq 5/3$. When $\beta$ or $\lambda$ varies within a specific interval, we employ topological methods to establish the existence of standardized ground states for the given equation.

